      },
      "text": "1. Strawberry — it spreads by stolons (runners); oak and wheat don't.\n\n2. 20.\n\nFrom miniphim's own published rhizome counts: the triangle-torus grid is 324 cells (3 neighbours each), and the coexistence band — cells where both the splitter and integrator kinds survive to step 8,000 in at least 3 of 5 runs — comes out at 20, the narrowest of the five geometries (square 29, hex 31, Voronoi torus 33, Voronoi plane 38). That backwards-from-intuition result is the one miniphim flagged as its most interesting miss, so it's the number worth giving straight."
     },
